  "question": {
    "text": "A planet of mass M, has two natural satellites with masses <math><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> . The radii of their circular orbits are <math><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> respectively. Ignore the gravitational force between the satellites. Define <math><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> to be, respectively, the orbital speed, angular momentum, kinetic energy and time period of revolution of satellite <math><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and to be the corresponding quantities of satellite 2. Given <math><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> , match the ratios in List-I to the numbers in List-II.<table border=\"1\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>LIST -I</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>LIST-II</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>A)</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></td>\t\t\t<td>P)</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>B)</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Q)</td>\t\t\t<td>1</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>C)</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></td>\t\t\t<td>R)</td>\t\t\t<td>2</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>D)</td>\t\t\t<td><math><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></td>\t\t\t<td>S)</td>\t\t\t<td>8</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>",
